<ArticleLayout title="Check Local Generator Service Before You Buy" description="A location-specific method for checking authorized commissioning, warranty work and emergency support without invented network scores." category="Research" categoryHref="/research/" published="2026-10-07" updated="2026-10-07" readingTime="6 min read" toc={[]} sources={[]}>
<p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Confirm who can commission and repair your exact model before accepting a proposal. A listing in a dealer locator does not establish emergency availability or warranty authorization. We currently publish no measured network scores or verified service-location dataset.</p>
<h2>Start with official manufacturer dealer and service locators</h2>
<p>These are manufacturer-controlled directories, not an independent endorsement, proof of a technician's availability or a verified local-service dataset. Confirm the current product, service category, and ZIP code directly with each provider.</p>
<ul>
  <li><a href="https://www.generac.com/link/b1360627d34446d092fdc4c35e8d34b9.aspx/" rel="external noopener noreferrer">Generac standby dealer locator</a> — use the maintenance/service filter for your area.</li>
  <li><a href="https://www.kohlerhomeenergy.rehlko.com/find-a-dealer" rel="external noopener noreferrer">KOHLER/Rehlko home-generator dealers</a> — check installation and service coverage.</li>
  <li><a href="https://www.championpowerequipment.com/dealer-locator/" rel="external noopener noreferrer">Champion home standby dealer locator</a> — check the standby installer/dealer category, not portable-generator retailers.</li>
  <li><a href="https://energy.briggsandstratton.com/en-us/residential/where-to-buy/dealer-locator" rel="external noopener noreferrer">Briggs &amp; Stratton Energy Solutions dealer locator</a> — distinguish sales-only providers from factory-trained service.</li>
  <li><a href="https://www.cummins.com/en-eu/na/generators/home-standby/find-a-dealer" rel="external noopener noreferrer">Cummins home standby dealer locator</a> — filter the location's home/small-business sales and repair capability.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Independence:</strong> These links are provided solely as service-research starting points. HomeGeneratorGuide receives no lead payment from these links and does not represent those manufacturers or dealers.</p>
<h2>Build a dated local record</h2><ol><li>Choose your metro or privacy-safe ZIP prefix and a search radius in miles. Record the date and manufacturer locator URL.</li><li>Deduplicate branches and overlapping listings; separate sales-only dealers, installers and authorized service providers.</li><li>Ask each provider whether it commissions your exact model and performs manufacturer warranty work. Record a direct source or documented reply, not an assumption.</li><li>Ask about storm-week response, after-hours coverage, travel limits, diagnostic fees and parts availability. Unanswered questions remain unknown.</li></ol>
<h2>Three questions to ask before paying a deposit</h2>
<ol><li>Will your team commission and service the <strong>exact model and ATS</strong> I am buying? Show any required authorization and registration in writing.</li><li>Who pays for warranty diagnosis, labor, travel and replacement parts, and is emergency coverage promised or only subject to availability?</li><li>If your company cannot attend during a major outage, which other qualified local provider can take over and what are their terms?</li></ol>
<h2>The comparison worksheet</h2><table class="mobile-card-table"><caption>Questions for each candidate provider</caption><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Evidence to request</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Authorization</th><td>Exact brand/model capability and dated manufacturer confirmation</td></tr><tr><th>Commissioning</th><td>Startup, testing and registration scope in the proposal</td></tr><tr><th>Warranty</th><td>Who files claims and which travel, labor and diagnostic charges remain yours</td></tr><tr><th>Emergency service</th><td>Written terms, service area and any response commitment</td></tr><tr><th>Backup option</th><td>Another qualified provider if the first is unavailable</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>What a future study can report</h2><p>A dated count of observed locations within a stated radius, with known capabilities and missing responses. It cannot promise future response time, rank national reliability or treat a missing listing as proof that service does not exist. Locator coverage, outdated listings and nonresponse must be disclosed.</p><p><strong>Buyer verdict:</strong> Keep a model on your shortlist when the relevant local service scope is documented. Pause the purchase if no provider can confirm who handles startup and warranty work. Compare that written scope in the <a href="/planning/quotes/">quote planner</a>.</p>
